    "durationMs": 318199,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `main.go` — entry point with `migrate` and `serve` subcommands; migrations are embedded in the binary\n- `internal/store` — pgx v5 connection pool and repository: `Create`, `GetByCode`, `RegisterClick`, `List`, plus a migration runner that tracks applied versions in `schema_migrations`\n- `internal/api` — chi v5.2.1 router with `POST /links`, `GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}`, and JSON error handlers\n- `migrations/001_create_links.sql` — `links` table with a unique `code` constraint\n- `start.sh` — builds, applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; `README.md` documents startup and the API\n\n**Verified end-to-end against real Postgres** (all via `sh start.sh`):\n- Generated codes match the 4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` format; submitted URLs returned unchanged; custom codes round-trip\n- `409` on duplicate custom code; `422` for malformed JSON, missing/invalid url (no scheme, no host, `ftp://`, space-in-host), and invalid codes (too short/long, bad chars); boundary 4- and 20-char codes accepted\n- Redirects return `302` with the exact stored `Location` and unknown codes/routes return JSON `404`\n- List returns ascending creation order with correct `total` (and `\"items\":[]` when empty)\n- Clicks survive a server restart (2 clicks → restart → still 2), and 50 parallel redirects incremented exactly once each (3 + 50 = 53) via atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING url`\n- Second `start.sh` run skips the already-applied migration (idempotent)\n\nThe database was reset to a pristine migrated-empty state afterward, `gofmt`/`go vet` are clean, chi is still pinned at v5.2.1, and no server is left running."
